namespace {{NAMESPACE}};

/// <summary>
/// The treatment names this model knows about. These strings are a contract with two files
/// outside the C# project and must match both exactly:
///
/// <list type="bullet">
///   <item><description>the <c>treatment_name</c> column of the <c>treatments</c> sheet in
///   <c>domain_model_setup.xlsx</c>, and</description></item>
///   <item><description>the budget category columns in the client's <c>inputs\budgets.xlsx</c> -
///   indirectly, via the <c>budget_category</c> column of that same <c>treatments</c>
///   sheet.</description></item>
/// </list>
///
/// <para>Both mismatches are caught, and neither is caught early. A name that does not match the
/// bundle throws partway through a run; a <c>budget_category</c> with no column in
/// <c>budgets.xlsx</c> fails the run at setup, naming the treatment, before a single period is
/// modelled. Loud is better than silent, but a run that dies at setup still costs the engineer
/// the round trip - so keep the strings in one place and let <c>jcass-dm check</c> find both
/// before you upload.</para>
///
/// <para><b>Adding a treatment</b> is a constant here, a bundle row, a trigger, and a reset arm:</para>
/// <list type="number">
///   <item><description>Add the <c>public const string</c> below.</description></item>
///   <item><description><c>jcass-dm add-treatment &lt;bundle&gt; --name &lt;that exact string&gt;
///   --budget-category &lt;a column in budgets.xlsx&gt;</c></description></item>
///   <item><description>Decide when it fires, and what it costs, in <see cref="TreatmentsTrigger"/>.</description></item>
///   <item><description>Handle it in <see cref="Resetter"/>. The <c>default:</c> arm there throws,
///   so a treatment you forget fails loudly rather than doing nothing.</description></item>
///   <item><description>Add its rate to the <c>unit_rates</c> set in <c>inputs\lookups.xlsx</c>.</description></item>
/// </list>
///
/// <example>
/// <code>
/// /// &lt;summary&gt;Partial intervention: restores surface condition, does not renew the asset.&lt;/summary&gt;
/// public const string Repair = "repair";
/// </code>
/// The constant's name is for your C#; the string is what the bundle, the budget and the outputs
/// all see. They do not have to look alike, but the string has to match the bundle character for
/// character - including case, and including any trailing space you cannot see.
/// </example>
/// </summary>
